CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_reference
COMMENT 'Shared code sets and classifications used across all domains, plus the generated data dictionary. Reference data is versioned with the model: allowed values live in the specs, not in anyone''s head.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_org
COMMENT 'The group''s own legal-entity structure - the reporting hierarchy every other domain hangs off. Solvency II, IFRS 17 and statutory accounts all report at solo (subsidiary) and group (consolidated) level; this domain is what makes that distinction real rather than assumed.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_finance
COMMENT 'The finance function proper - a real double-entry general ledger (chart of accounts, balanced journals, accounting periods), the operational sub-ledgers (premium, claims, commission, expense, receivables), regulatory and actuarial measures (Solvency II, IFRS 17), financial-statement structure, budget and FX. Everything a CFO org runs on.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_investment
COMMENT 'The asset side of the balance sheet - investment holdings, valuations and income. Roughly half an insurer''s balance sheet; without it there is no balance sheet and no ALM conversation.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_party
COMMENT 'People and organisations, and the roles they play in the business (insured, broker, cedant, reinsurer, claimant). A party exists once; relationships are roles.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_policy
COMMENT 'Insurance contracts and their composition - policies, coverages, insured objects and premium transactions.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_claim
COMMENT 'Claims against policies and their financial development - reserves, payments and recoveries as transactions, never as overwritten balances.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_reinsurance
COMMENT 'Outward and inward reinsurance - treaties, cessions and recoveries linking the direct book to reinsurers.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_reserving
COMMENT 'Actuarial reserving as a governed semantic layer over claim transactions - loss-development triangles, chain-ladder and Bornhuetter-Ferguson estimates, IBNR and ultimate losses by accident year. Triangles are derived by summation over claim movements, never stored; the method used is a recorded, attestable choice. The spreadsheet workflow, done on the platform: reproducible, reconciling to source, and answerable in Genie.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_product
COMMENT 'Machine-readable products - offered coverages, underwriting questions and appetite rules as data, so any channel (human, aggregator or buyer agent) can discover, quote and be decided against the same rules.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_enrichment
COMMENT 'External and derived risk data joined to the canonical model - telematics, credit, geospatial hazard, postcode, market benchmarks, demographics and sanctions screening. These are third-party or derived attributes about a policy, party or insured object, kept as governed, classified data rather than scattered feature tables. Pricing and underwriting both draw on them; modelling them once, with data classification, is what lets those workbenches share risk signal instead of each re-sourcing it.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_model
COMMENT 'Machine-learning and analytical models as governed assets - the model, its versions, the features it consumes, the scores it produces and its monitoring metrics. The layer represents AI the way it represents data: every score traces to a model version, every feature to a definition and a classification. This is what makes model governance a first-class part of the semantic layer, not a side system.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_pricing
COMMENT 'The rating structure - factors, their levels and relativities, engine configurations and the derived factor contributions on a quote or policy. Pricing decisions become explainable data: a quoted premium decomposes into the factors and relativities that produced it, and the engine config cites the model version behind it.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_distribution
COMMENT 'How business reaches the insurer - channels and intermediary remuneration, transactional and disclosable.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_conduct
COMMENT 'Fair treatment made measurable - complaints per FCA groupings, through to ombudsman referral and redress.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_content
COMMENT 'Governed unstructured content - wordings, schedules, evidence, slips - with extracted text searchable under the same governance as rows.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_events
COMMENT 'The append-only business event stream - the near-real-time face of the model and the feed for monitoring agents.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_life
COMMENT 'Life business - grouped model points, governed assumption sets, economic scenario sets and valuation runs. Life policies themselves are ordinary policies with life lines of business.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_exchange
COMMENT 'Canonical data-exchange objects (bordereau lines, submissions) and the landing zone for inbound counterparty data before mapping to the canonical model.';

CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS lr_serverless_aws_us_catalog.bricksurance_semantics
COMMENT 'Business metrics defined once over the canonical model - gross written premium, net earned premium, incurred, loss ratio, combined ratio. Physicalised as metric views where the platform supports them.';
